          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal words directly avow the narrator's present love for Maria. They answer her request for assurance that his apparent change is real rather than temporary or merely sexual, and the oath-like introductory comparison presents the avowal as especially truthful and considered.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.93,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the avowal also affirms an enduring relational undertaking: he positions himself as loving Maria through pleasure and hardship and as intending to share a long life with her. These are not merely unrelated nearby promises. They immediately restate and specify what his answer to her question about permanence means, giving the focal avowal substantial commitment force. T remains dominant because the exact marked words are most directly a declaration of emotional state.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"For det er jo sandt, ikke noget, Du imorgen fortryder, ikke\\nnoget, Du nu bilder Dig ind, fordi Du har længtes en Smule efter din\\nElskerinde?\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"Although the reunion is highly emotional, the focal expression is a deliberate answer to Maria's question, supported by an oath-like assurance and reasoned elaboration. The evidence does not present it as a reflexive cry or affective discharge beyond its avowing and undertaking functions.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.88,\"reason\":\"The focal expression's relevant force is adequately represented by its strong avowal and contextually established affirmation of an enduring bond. The supplied scene does not support a distinct residual speech-act function.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At their reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent love is genuine, lasting, and more than renewed desire for his lover. He answers her directly with the focal avowal and immediately defines that love as enduring through changing circumstances and involving a long shared life.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The same turn affirms an undertaking to love Maria in pleasure and hardship, in ordinary and festive life, and to live with her for a very long time before ultimately dying with her. Its precise practical terms are not specified, but it clearly answers her concern about permanence. Maria's response supplies positive uptake: she understands him as speaking truthfully and weeps from happiness. The later wedding supports the narrative trajectory but is not needed to manufacture undertaking force for the focal occurrence.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work with sufficient confidence to identify it.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly establishes the represented avowal, commitment framing, affection, and immediate uptake. It cannot independently prove inner sincerity as a fact beyond the narrator's representation, nor does it fully specify the practical terms of the relationship undertaking.\"}"
